  "final_message": "`compute_fee(1000, \"gold\")` returns 480. I worked it out by hand and got the same result by running the function.\n\n1. `service2.compute_fee` imports only `pricing.base_fee` and `discounts.apply_discount`.\n2. `base_fee(1000)` is 500 + 1000 // 10 = 600.\n3. `apply_discount(600, \"gold\")` uses a 20% discount: 600 \u2212 (600 \u00d7 20) // 100 = 480.\n\nNothing imports `decoy_tax.py` (25% for gold) or `decoy_shipping.py`, so they don't change the result.\n\nANSWER: 480",
